WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.119
Retrieval augmented generation supplies selected external evidence to a model before it

00:00:05.119 --> 00:00:05.546
answers.

00:00:05.696 --> 00:00:12.951
The pipeline is query preparation, authorized retrieval, optional reranking, context assembly, generation,

00:00:12.951 --> 00:00:14.160
and verification.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:18.414
Retrieval quality and answer quality are separate: the right document may be

00:00:18.414 --> 00:00:20.808
retrieved while the model still misstates it.

00:00:20.958 --> 00:00:25.824
Require source identifiers that correspond to supplied evidence and make uncertainty explicit

00:00:25.824 --> 00:00:28.663
when the evidence is missing or contradictory.

00:00:28.813 --> 00:00:32.432
A citation is useful only if it supports the adjacent claim.

00:00:32.582 --> 00:00:35.570
Do not treat a plausible-looking source label as proof.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:41.606
Test questions that are answerable, unanswerable, outdated, ambiguous, and adversarial.

00:00:41.756 --> 00:00:46.996
For A100, the order record supports delayed status and policy v1 supports

00:00:46.996 --> 00:00:48.306
manual support review.

00:00:48.456 --> 00:00:51.946
Neither supports an exact delivery date or an approved refund.

00:00:52.096 --> 00:00:55.890
A grounded answer states the supported facts and stops at that boundary.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.789
An answer that adds delivery tomorrow fails even if it cites the

00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:00.414
order record.

00:01:00.564 --> 00:01:05.566
Create a 20-question evaluation set with five deliberately unanswerable questions.

00:01:05.716 --> 00:01:10.503
Grade source correctness, claim support, and appropriate abstention separately.

00:01:10.653 --> 00:01:13.831
Include one document containing malicious instructions.

00:01:13.981 --> 00:01:17.016
Use a human-reviewed answer key for important facts.

00:01:17.166 --> 00:01:21.197
Automated model graders can assist but need calibration against that key.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.912
Count unsupported claims even when the answer is otherwise useful.

00:01:25.062 --> 00:01:29.249
Preserve the adversarial document as data and verify that it does not

00:01:29.249 --> 00:01:30.296
change tool permissions.

00:01:30.446 --> 00:01:31.117
Question.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:33.398
Does RAG eliminate hallucinations?

00:01:33.548 --> 00:01:34.125
Answer.

00:01:34.275 --> 00:01:34.758
No.

00:01:34.908 --> 00:01:40.121
It improves access to relevant evidence but retrieval, interpretation, and generation can

00:01:40.121 --> 00:01:40.989
still fail.

00:01:41.139 --> 00:01:41.811
Question.

00:01:41.961 --> 00:01:43.716
When should the assistant abstain?

00:01:43.866 --> 00:01:44.442
Answer.

00:01:44.592 --> 00:01:49.052
When authorized evidence cannot support the requested claim or the available sources

00:01:49.052 --> 00:01:50.911
conflict without a resolvable rule.
